            <ArticleTitle>Myelolipoma of the adrenal gland diagnosis and management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>457-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myelolipoma of the adrenal gland is a rare benign tumor. It is diagnosed incidentally in most cases because of its non-functioning nature, unless it causes symptoms due to its size. It has specific sonographic and computed tomographic features. A case is presented, magnetic resonance findings are reported for the first time and a review of the literature is conducted.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
